# Phala / dstack documentation gate

Before implementing or changing anything that touches Phala Cloud, dstack, CVM
deploy, compose-hash, encrypted envs, custom domains / dstack-ingress, GHCR, or
attestation packaging:

1. Read `docs/market-dstack.md` (repo packaging source of truth).
2. Fetch https://docs.phala.com/llms.txt and pick the pages that match the task
   (deploy CLI, env vars, private registry, networking, custom domain, KMS,
   attestation, etc.).
3. Read those pages (and any dstack-examples links cited in `docs/market-dstack.md`)
   **before** writing code, compose, or operator commands.
4. Prefer quoted upstream behavior over memory; if our packaging doc and upstream
   disagree, stop and reconcile explicitly.

Do not invent Phala CLI flags, `allowed_envs`, DNS provider vars, or app-compose
fields from prior chat alone.
